WEBVTT

00:28:57.663 --> 00:29:01.996
This tendency for connectivity brings us
to one last surprise from Emily's studies.

00:29:02.663 --> 00:29:06.246
During moments of uncertainty, but
especially economic uncertainty,

00:29:06.496 --> 00:29:08.913
we tend to rethink our relationships
with others.

00:29:09.454 --> 00:29:12.788
We become less individualistic
and more civically minded.

00:29:13.621 --> 00:29:18.788
Emily has found an ingenious way to
measure that through pop music.

00:29:22.121 --> 00:29:24.538
When we're struggling through
bad economic times,

00:29:24.788 --> 00:29:26.538
we're drawn to different lyrics

00:29:26.996 --> 00:29:28.454
in popular American music,

00:29:28.454 --> 00:29:32.829
you're more likely to see first person
plural pronouns like we us.